5. THE OTHER ROUTE: the PROVED increment bound [P56], maximised over
   placements.  U(P) = TOTAL(P) + sum of Bmax(m) for the cubes still to
   come.  Bmax(m) = max cells that m other cubes' 6m face planes can cut
   on the new cube's surface.  CRUDE cap derived here, NOT from the
   project's own Lemma 1a -- two planes meet ∂C_new in <= 2 points, each
   plane curve has <= 6 vertices on the cube's 12 edges, degrees <= 4,
   components <= 6m+1.  Every step is generous; this is an upper bound on
   an upper bound and is quoted only to see whether the ROUTE could prune.
==============================================================================
   m  crude Bmax(m)  actual increment   ratio
   3            442               120     3.7x
   4            730               210     3.5x
   5           1090               334     3.3x
   6           1522               490     3.1x
   7           2026               678     3.0x

  A bound 3-5x above the achieved increment, compounding over every
  remaining cube, cannot prune a branch whose completion is near the
  record.  The route is not refuted -- it needs a TIGHT Bmax, which is
  the open item, not the framework.

